description:  The Medical Grasper project focused on developing an assistive device for individuals with arthritis to grip objects with minimal finger movement. I collaborated with a team to build and evaluate an Arduino-based prototype integrating a photosensor and servomotor to detect finger motion and actuate the grasper. I also designed a forearm support component in SolidWorks to improve device stability, alignment, and user comfort.
